  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following Deepavali celebrations, several Indian cities, particularly New Delhi, experienced a sharp decline in air quality due to the widespread use of firecrackers and meteorological conditions that trapped pollutants. Delhi recorded an average Air Quality Index of 376, with some monitoring stations reporting levels exceeding 400. This has resulted in dense smog and limited visibility across the capital. A political dispute has emerged regarding the accuracy of air quality reports, following claims by opposition figures that PM2.5 readings were unavailable at a significant portion of monitoring stations during the event. While some political groups allege that air quality data is being manipulated, others have characterized the situation as a conspiracy, leading to heightened scrutiny over the effectiveness of existing pollution control measures and monitoring infrastructure in the region.",
